{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/library/8128","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":"8128","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"call number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300311706"}],"content":"N7350 .A277","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"Exhibition of Japanese painting and sculpture sponsored by the Government of Japan: National Gallery of Art, Washington; the Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York; Museum of Fine Arts, Boston; the Art Institute of Chicago; Seattle Art Museum, Seattle.","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"s.n.","id":"actor/s-n","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"_label":"1953","begin_of_the_begin":"1953-01-01T00:00:00Z","end_of_the_end":"1953-01-01T00:00:00Z","type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"inscription statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435414"}],"content":"abq copy : good condition.|grl copy : good condition.|SColl abq : Annotation by unknown on front cover : e.|SColl abq : Embossed stamp on front loose endpaper : Georgia O'Keeffe / Abiquiu, New Mexico.|SColl abq : errata slip.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"Ephemera found between pp. 114-115 : Newspaper clipping : image of Monkeys in a Bamboo Grove as depicted on p. 131, undated, unknown source.\nEphemera found between pp. 120-121 : Newspaper clipping : image of Wind and Waves as depicted on p. 121, undated, unknown source.\nEphemera found between pp. 162-163 : Newspaper clipping : image of Pine Trees in Snow as depicted on p. 163, undated, unknown source.\nEphemera found between pp. 52-53 : Newspaper clipping : The Best from Japan by A.B.L., January 25, 1953, unknown source ; features image of Chigo Daishi as depicted on p. 53.\nEphemera found between pp. 60-61 : Newspaper clipping : image of Inga koy as depicted on p. 61, undated, unknown source.\nEphemera found between pp. 62-63 : Newspaper clipping : image of Animals as depicted on p. 63, undated, unknown source.\nEphemera found between pp. 90-91 : Newspaper clipping : image of Priest Myo-e as depicted on p. 91, undated, unknown source.\nGeorgia O'Keeffe Personal Library.\nEphemera found between pp. 18-19 : Five blank postcards from the Museum of Fine Arts, Boston featuring 13th century Japanese art.\nEphemera found inside back cover : Blank postcard from the Museum of Fine Arts, Boston featuring 13th century Japanese art.\nFrom Georgia O'Keeffe's Ghost Ranch library.\nOriginally housed in manila folder labeled : 44 Bank.\nAssembled under the auspices of the Commission for the Protection of Cultural Properties.","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}